# Weld one payload to the robot base (bridge_node's /attach_payload).
# Refused unless the payload's center is within the node's attach distance
# limit (the attach_max_distance parameter, default 0.30 m), refused unless
# the robot is facing it -- the payload's centre within the attach_max_angle
# parameter (default 20 deg) either side of the red arrow on the robot's top
# plate -- refused unless the robot is right up against it when the
# attach_max_gap parameter is set (task3a: the robot's front within 0.05 m of
# the payload), and refused if that payload, or any other, is already attached.
# A weld named "weld_<payload_name>" (body1=robot base, body2=payload_name)
# must exist in the loaded model; see task3a.xml.
#
# Release it again with hb_description/srv/DetachPayload.

string payload_name   # e.g. "payload_alpha"
---
bool success
string message
float64 distance      # robot-to-payload center distance at the time of the call, in metres
